  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "[\"Only the front-oblique exterior is independently photographed in the successfully accessed paper. Far flank and depth inferred from continuous dextral shell construction; use smooth conservative continuation, do not fabricate hidden damage. Four renders are presentation/evaluation views, not claims of four observed specimen views.\", \"10 approximate visible turns including tiny apical turns; erosion limits exact count. Overall ratio and shallow flanks are more important than an invented exact turn count.\", \"Aperture cavity depth, missing thin lip and precise internal folds are not resolved. Do not invent deep anatomy or recreate Fig5B cross-section in an exterior model.\", \"The literal extremely tall wording is unsupported by selected type-species specimen; maintain real2.7:1 ratio. Historical Nerinea usage included taxa reassigned to Eunerinea; do not transfer those shapes.\", \"Colour is an artistic stone palette, not a biological colour claim.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"target_height_Z\": 0.059, \"target_width_X\": 0.022, \"target_depth_Y\": 0.021, \"evidence\": \"Fig5C: paper states scale bars10mm. In rendered page1172x1640, bar x678–727=49px; fossil y242–530=288px, width about108px. Thus projected height58.8mm and width22.0mm. Depth21mm is inferred from a rounded shell body, not directly measured.\", \"engineering_tolerance\": \"Height56–62mm, width20–24mm, inferred depth19–24mm. These are design tolerances, not biological confidence limits.\"} Original inventory adjective very tall/extremely tall had no numeric ratio and was provisional. Verified type species specimen is about 2.7:1, not a 5:1 needle. Root approved evidence-led correction 2026-10-22 20:25 UTC. Preserve real Nerinea proportions; do not borrow Eunerinea, stretch the specimen or claim the original extreme adjective is proven.",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：[\"Only the front-oblique exterior is independently photographed in the successfully accessed paper. Far flank and depth inferred from continuous dextral shell construction; use smooth conservative continuation, do not fabricate hidden damage. Four renders are presentation/evaluation views, not claims of four observed specimen views.\", \"10 approximate visible turns including tiny apical turns; erosion limits exact count. Overall ratio and shallow flanks are more important than an invented exact turn count.\", \"Aperture cavity depth, missing thin lip and precise internal folds are not resolved. Do not invent deep anatomy or recreate Fig5B cross-section in an exterior model.\", \"The literal extremely tall wording is unsupported by selected type-species specimen; maintain real2.7:1 ratio. Historical Nerinea usage included taxa reassigned to Eunerinea; do not transfer those shapes.\", \"Colour is an artistic stone palette, not a biological colour claim.\"] {\"unit\": \"metre\", \"target_height_Z\": 0.059, \"target_width_X\": 0.022, \"target_depth_Y\": 0.021, \"evidence\": \"Fig5C: paper states scale bars10mm. In rendered page1172x1640, bar x678–727=49px; fossil y242–530=288px, width about108px. Thus projected height58.8mm and width22.0mm. Depth21mm is inferred from a rounded shell body, not directly measured.\", \"engineering_tolerance\": \"Height56–62mm, width20–24mm, inferred depth19–24mm. These are design tolerances, not biological confidence limits.\"} Original inventory adjective very tall/extremely tall had no numeric ratio and was provisional. Verified type species specimen is about 2.7:1, not a 5:1 needle. Root approved evidence-led correction 2026-10-22 20:25 UTC. Preserve real Nerinea proportions; do not borrow Eunerinea, stretch the specimen or claim the original extreme adjective is proven."
  },
